# Sideload after changes

When you finish implementing or fixing something in this Android project:

1. Build the debug APK: `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug` (use `JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-17-openjdk-amd64` and `ANDROID_HOME=~/Android/Sdk` if needed).
2. Sideload to the test tablet: `adb connect <host:port>` then `adb -s <host:port> install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk`.
3. Mention sideload success in the summary.

Do this on every completed task that touches the app, unless the user explicitly says not to sideload.

## Physical tablet — do NOT reboot or restart system services

The test tablet uses **wireless adb** (port changes on reconnect). Never on a physical device:

- `adb reboot`
- `scripts/grant-usb-permission.sh` (runs `killall system_server` on emulators — breaks wireless adb on tablets)
- `scripts/grant-emulator-usb-host.sh` (explicit reboot)
- Any command that restarts `system_server` or waits for boot

Sideload is **install -r only**. Grant USB permission in the app UI when prompted.
